    <item>
      <title>2026 Democracy Summit at Blackburn Center (Armour J. Blackburn University Center)</title>
      <description><![CDATA[<div>  <img src="https://localist-images.azureedge.net/photos/53851266996443/huge/35b2a6ea9604642a989f0cb6f77a23f481acbbdf.jpg" style="width: 100%;" />  <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;"><strong>Tue, 06 Oct 2026</strong></div>  <div><p>The Center for Journalism &amp; Democracy at Howard University will host the 2026 Democracy Summit on Oct. 6 from 8:30 a.m. to 5 p.m. ET at the Howard University Blackburn Center. The summit will bring together journalists, media executives, civic leaders, journalism students and scholars. </p>

<p> </p>

<p>As journalists and newsrooms across the country fight to defend press freedom, the Democracy Summit will feature substantive conversations examining the growing threats to journalism and democratic institutions and how journalists and news organizations can respond.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>As the 2026 midterm elections approach, more than 300 newsroom executives, domestic and international journalists, legal scholars and democracy leaders will gather for a full day of learning, strategy and preparation focused on press freedom, election coverage and democratic resilience.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Here's what you can look forward to:</p>

<p>Conversations with the nation's leading voices in media and journalism</p>

<p>Timely discussions on press attacks, democratic erosion and the fight to defend journalism</p>

<p>Exchanges with international journalists sharing lessons on democratic backsliding and recovery</p>

<p>A real-time election reporting scenario to stress-test your decision desk preparedness</p>

<p>A live newsroom simulation testing editorial and legal judgment</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Registration for the 2026 Democracy Summit has closed. The 2026 Democracy Summit will be livestreamed for the public on YouTube @c4jdhowardu.</p>

<p><a href="https://events.howard.edu/event/2026-democracy-summit">View on site</a> | <a href="mailto:?subject=I found an interesting event%3A 2026 Democracy Summit&amp;body=I found an interesting event you may like%3A%0A%0A%0ADate%3A Oct 6%2C 2026%0A%0ADescription%3A%0AThe Center for Journalism %26 Democracy at Howard University will host the 2026 Democracy Summit on Oct. 6 from 8%3A30 a.m. to 5 p.m. ET at the Howard University Blackburn Center. The summit will bring together journalists%2C media executives%2C civic leaders%2C journalism students and scholars. %0A%0A %0A%0AAs journalists and newsrooms across the country fight to defend press freedom%2C the Democracy Summit will feature substantive conversations examining the growing threats to journalism and democratic institutions and how journalists and news organizations can respond.%0A%0A %0A%0AAs the 2026 midterm elections approach%2C more than 300 newsroom executives%2C domestic and international journalists%2C legal scholars and democracy leaders will gather for a full day of learning%2C strategy and preparation focused on press freedom%2C election coverage and democratic resilience.%0A%0A %0A%0AHere%27s what you can look forward to%3A%0A%0AConversations with the nation%27s leading voices in media and journalism%0A%0ATimely discussions on press attacks%2C democratic erosion and the fight to defend journalism%0A%0AExchanges with international journalists sharing lessons on democratic backsliding and recovery%0A%0AA real-time election reporting scenario to stress-test your decision desk preparedness%0A%0AA live newsroom simulation testing editorial and legal judgment%0A%0A %0A%0ARegistration for the 2026 Democracy Summit has closed. The 2026 Democracy Summit will be livestreamed for the public on YouTube %40c4jdhowardu.%0A%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fevents.howard.edu%2Fevent%2F2026-democracy-summit%0A">Email this event</a></p></div></div>]]></description>
