      <title>AI Jobs and Skills Across the States Webinar: How is Ohio Preparing People for an AI-Enabled Workforce?</title>
      <description><![CDATA[<div>  <img src="https://localist-images.azureedge.net/photos/54135135579113/huge/25d2946f979e72f678254521895d995748f6be20.jpg" style="width: 100%;" />  <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;"><strong>Tue, 06 Oct 2026</strong></div>  <div><p>The AI Jobs and Skills Across the States webinar explores how states are advancing AI, preparing their workforces, and expanding opportunity. This session highlights Ohio’s work at the intersection of AI, education, workforce development, and economic opportunity and offers a timely opportunity to learn how AI is reshaping jobs, workforce skills, and education pathways.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Date: Tuesday, October 6, 2026
<br>Time: 4:00–5:30 p.m. ET</p>

<p>Featured Speaker: Katrina Flory, State Chief Information Officer and Assistant Director, Office of Information Technology, State of Ohio</p>

<p>Format: Virtual via Zoom Webinar</p>

<p>Register Here: <a href="https://howard.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_pziaq6EMSd6ZsGLx3CbQUQ#/registration">https://howard.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_pziaq6EMSd6ZsGLx3CbQUQ#/registration</a></p>

<p> </p>

<p>The webinar will include brief framing remarks, interactive discussion, and collaborative synthesis to explore the central question: How is AI changing jobs, the skills people need, and the opportunities ahead?</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Come hear what is happening in Ohio, learn from perspectives across sectors, and add your own insights to this important conversation. </p>

<p> </p>

<p>AI Jobs and Skills Across the States is organized through the NSF-supported Research Coordination Network on Assessing and Predicting Job Outcomes in AI (RCN APJO-AI). Insights from these discussions will contribute to national conversations on AI workforce development, talent pathways, and regional innovation ecosystems.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Learn more: <a href="https://www.aijobsrcn.org/events">https://www.aijobsrcn.org/events</a></p>

<p> </p>

<p>This material is based upon work supported by the U.S. National Science Foundation (NSF) under Grant No. 2537092.  Any opinions, findings, and conclusions or recommendations expressed in this material are those of the author(s) and do not necessarily reflect the views of the NSF.</p>

<p><a href="https://events.howard.edu/event/ai-jobs-and-skills-across-the-states-webinar-how-is-ohio-preparing-people-for-an-ai-enabled-workforce">View on site</a> | <a href="mailto:?subject=I found an interesting event%3A AI Jobs and Skills Across the States Webinar%3A How is Ohio Preparing People for an AI-Enabled Workforce%3F&amp;body=I found an interesting event you may like%3A%0A%0A%0ADate%3A Oct 6%2C 2026%0A%0ADescription%3A%0AThe AI Jobs and Skills Across the States webinar explores how states are advancing AI%2C preparing their workforces%2C and expanding opportunity. This session highlights Ohio%E2%80%99s work at the intersection of AI%2C education%2C workforce development%2C and economic opportunity and offers a timely opportunity to learn how AI is reshaping jobs%2C workforce skills%2C and education pathways.%0A%0A %0A%0ADate%3A Tuesday%2C October 6%2C 2026%0ATime%3A 4%3A00%E2%80%935%3A30 p.m. ET%0A%0AFeatured Speaker%3A Katrina Flory%2C State Chief Information Officer and Assistant Director%2C Office of Information Technology%2C State of Ohio%0A%0AFormat%3A Virtual via Zoom Webinar%0A%0ARegister Here%3A https%3A%2F%2Fhoward.zoom.us%2Fwebinar%2Fregister%2FWN_pziaq6EMSd6ZsGLx3CbQUQ%23%2Fregistration%0A%0A %0A%0AThe webinar will include brief framing remarks%2C interactive discussion%2C and collaborative synthesis to explore the central question%3A How is AI changing jobs%2C the skills people need%2C and the opportunities ahead%3F%0A%0A %0A%0ACome hear what is happening in Ohio%2C learn from perspectives across sectors%2C and add your own insights to this important conversation. %0A%0A %0A%0AAI Jobs and Skills Across the States is organized through the NSF-supported Research Coordination Network on Assessing and Predicting Job Outcomes in AI %28RCN APJO-AI%29. Insights from these discussions will contribute to national conversations on AI workforce development%2C talent pathways%2C and regional innovation ecosystems.%0A%0A %0A%0ALearn more%3A https%3A%2F%2F